IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`
IMPORT `ea1-part3a-payment`

-- Tests for ea1-part3a-payment.l4 (ss 20 to 25).  Every expected value is written from
-- the text of the section (inputs/EmA1968.txt) before the function was run.
-- Calendar facts used: 1 January 2026 is a Thursday, so 1 February 2026 and 1 March 2026
-- are Sundays; 31 January 2026 is a Saturday.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 20 Fixation of salary period`
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the employer may fix periods in respect of which salary earned is payable` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the employer may fix periods in respect of which salary earned is payable` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): a period from 1 March ends by 31 March to be within one month.
`a period 1 to 31 March 2026` MEANS `Period of days` WITH `first day` IS Date 1 3 2026, `last day` IS Date 31 3 2026
`a period 1 March to 1 April 2026` MEANS `Period of days` WITH `first day` IS Date 1 3 2026, `last day` IS Date 1 4 2026
`a period 15 February to 14 March 2026` MEANS `Period of days` WITH `first day` IS Date 15 2 2026, `last day` IS Date 14 3 2026
`a period 15 February to 15 March 2026` MEANS `Period of days` WITH `first day` IS Date 15 2 2026, `last day` IS Date 15 3 2026
-- a period starting on 31 January: the next month has no 31st, so it ends on 28 February at the latest.
`a period 31 January to 28 February 2026` MEANS `Period of days` WITH `first day` IS Date 31 1 2026, `last day` IS Date 28 2 2026
`a period 31 January to 1 March 2026` MEANS `Period of days` WITH `first day` IS Date 31 1 2026, `last day` IS Date 1 3 2026
`a period 1 to 1 March 2026` MEANS `Period of days` WITH `first day` IS Date 1 3 2026, `last day` IS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the salary period does not exceed one month` `a period 1 to 31 March 2026` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the salary period does not exceed one month` `a period 1 March to 1 April 2026` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the salary period does not exceed one month` `a period 15 February to 14 March 2026` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the salary period does not exceed one month` `a period 15 February to 15 March 2026` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the salary period does not exceed one month` `a period 31 January to 28 February 2026` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the salary period does not exceed one month` `a period 31 January to 1 March 2026` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the salary period does not exceed one month` `a period 1 to 1 March 2026` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (3)
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the salary period is deemed to be one month` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(3) the salary period is deemed to be one month` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 20A Computation of salary for incomplete month's work`
-- (1): arguments are: monthly-rated, (a) began after the first day, (b) terminated before the end, (c) unpaid leave, (d) national service.
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) the employee has not completed a whole month of service for a reason in paragraphs (a) to (d)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) the employee has not completed a whole month of service for a reason in paragraphs (a) to (d)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) the employee has not completed a whole month of service for a reason in paragraphs (a) to (d)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) the employee has not completed a whole month of service for a reason in paragraphs (a) to (d)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none of the four reasons: "If a monthly-rated employee has not completed a whole month of service because" is an unmet "if": no (ruled 2026-11-05).
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) the employee has not completed a whole month of service for a reason in paragraphs (a) to (d)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a monthly-rated employee: the same "if" is unmet: no (ruled 2026-11-05).
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) the employee has not completed a whole month of service for a reason in paragraphs (a) to (d)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The formula.  A monthly-rated employee paid 3000 for the work and 200 in allowances of another kind, and 500 of overtime (the overtime is not part of the gross rate of pay).
`a monthly pay record` MEANS `Pay for a period` WITH `the amounts are for` IS `Pay is fixed for each month`, `pay for the work, with wage adjustments and increments` IS 3000, `overtime payments` IS 500, `bonus payments or annual wage supplements` IS 0, `commissions` IS 0, `productivity incentive payments` IS 0, `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment` IS 0, `travelling allowances` IS 0, `food allowances` IS 0, `housing allowances` IS 0, `allowances of any other kind` IS 200, `value of house accommodation, electricity, water, medical attendance or other amenity` IS 0, `value of a service excluded by order of the Minister` IS 0, `value of a travelling concession` IS 0, `employer's contributions on its own account to a pension fund or provident fund` IS 0, `gratuity payable on discharge or retirement` IS 0, `retrenchment benefit payable on retrenchment` IS 0
`a daily pay record` MEANS `Pay for a period` WITH `the amounts are for` IS `Pay is fixed for each day`, `pay for the work, with wage adjustments and increments` IS 100, `overtime payments` IS 0, `bonus payments or annual wage supplements` IS 0, `commissions` IS 0, `productivity incentive payments` IS 0, `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment` IS 0, `travelling allowances` IS 0, `food allowances` IS 0, `housing allowances` IS 0, `allowances of any other kind` IS 0, `value of house accommodation, electricity, water, medical attendance or other amenity` IS 0, `value of a service excluded by order of the Minister` IS 0, `value of a travelling concession` IS 0, `employer's contributions on its own account to a pension fund or provident fund` IS 0, `gratuity payable on discharge or retirement` IS 0, `retrenchment benefit payable on retrenchment` IS 0
-- gross rate of pay 3200; 20 days required; 5 worked: 3200 / 20 x 5 = 800.
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) the salary due for the month` `a monthly pay record` 20 5 EQUALS JUST 800
-- all 20 worked: the whole 3200.
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) the salary due for the month` `a monthly pay record` 20 20 EQUALS JUST 3200
-- none worked: nothing is due.
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) the salary due for the month` `a monthly pay record` 20 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- 5.5 days worked (see subsection (2)): 3200 / 20 x 5.5 = 880.
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) the salary due for the month` `a monthly pay record` 20 5.5 EQUALS JUST 880
-- the pay is not a monthly one: the formula is written for the monthly gross rate.
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) the salary due for the month` `a daily pay record` 20 5 EQUALS NOTHING
-- no days required to work: the formula divides by that number and gives no answer.
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) the salary due for the month` `a monthly pay record` 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): 4 days of more than 5 hours and 3 days of 5 hours or less: 4 + 1.5 = 5.5.
#ASSERT `s 20A(2) the number of days actually worked` 4 3 EQUALS 5.5
#ASSERT `s 20A(2) the number of days actually worked` 4 0 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `s 20A(2) the number of days actually worked` 0 1 EQUALS 0.5

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 21 Time of payment`
-- (1): the salary period ended on Saturday 31 January 2026; the 7th day after is Saturday 7 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the last day before the expiry of which the salary must be paid` (Date 31 1 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 7 2 2026)
-- the 7th day is a public holiday and the next day is a Sunday: the period includes the Monday, 9 February.
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the last day before the expiry of which the salary must be paid` (Date 31 1 2026) (LIST Date 7 2 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 9 2 2026)
-- the salary period ended on Wednesday 28 January 2026: the 7th day after is Wednesday 4 February.
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the last day before the expiry of which the salary must be paid` (Date 28 1 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 4 2 2026)
-- the 7th day after Sunday 1 February 2026... counting from the last day of the period: 1 February is excluded, so the 7th day is Sunday 8 February, which moves to Monday 9 February.
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the last day before the expiry of which the salary must be paid` (Date 1 2 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 9 2 2026)
-- arguments: last day of the period, the day paid, public holidays, additional payment for overtime.
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the salary was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the last day of the salary period` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 7 2 2026) EMPTY FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the salary was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the last day of the salary period` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 8 2 2026) EMPTY FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- with 7 February a public holiday, payment on Monday 9 February is in time and on 10 February is not.
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the salary was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the last day of the salary period` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 9 2 2026) (LIST Date 7 2 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the salary was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the last day of the salary period` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (LIST Date 7 2 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- paid early, before the period ended: still in time.
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the salary was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the last day of the salary period` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 25 1 2026) EMPTY FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an additional payment for overtime work is subsection (2)'s: subsection (1) is silent.
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the salary was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the last day of the salary period` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 7 2 2026) EMPTY TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) as a duty with 7 days: paid on the 7th day, fulfilled; on the 8th, breached (read the two traces).
#TRACE `s 21(1) the employer's duty to pay the salary earned` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 21(1) the employer` DOES `s 21(1) pay the salary earned` AT 7
#TRACE `s 21(1) the employer's duty to pay the salary earned` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 21(1) the employer` DOES `s 21(1) pay the salary earned` AT 8
-- (2): the salary period ended on Saturday 31 January 2026; 14 days after is Saturday 14 February.
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the last day by which the additional payments for overtime work must be paid` (Date 31 1 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 14 2 2026)
-- if 14 February is a public holiday: Sunday 15 February is excluded too, so Monday 16 February.
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the last day by which the additional payments for overtime work must be paid` (Date 31 1 2026) (LIST Date 14 2 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 16 2 2026)
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the additional payments for overtime work were paid not later than 14 days after the last day of the salary period` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 14 2 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 21(2) the additional payments for overtime work were paid not later than 14 days after the last day of the salary period` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 15 2 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 21(2) the employer's duty to pay the additional payments for overtime work` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 21(2) the employer` DOES `s 21(2) pay the additional payments for overtime work` AT 14
#TRACE `s 21(2) the employer's duty to pay the additional payments for overtime work` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 21(2) the employer` DOES `s 21(2) pay the additional payments for overtime work` AT 15
-- (3): paid on the day the contract was completed.
#ASSERT `s 21(3) the total salary due was paid on completion of the contract of service` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 21(3) the total salary due was paid on completion of the contract of service` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 11 1 2026))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 22 Payment on dismissal`
-- Dismissed on Thursday 5 February 2026.  Sunday 8 February is a rest day.
-- If it was possible to pay that day, the day is the dismissal day itself.
#ASSERT `s 22 the last day on which the total salary and any sum due must be paid` (Date 5 2 2026) FALSE (LIST Date 8 2 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 5 2 2026)
-- not possible; the 3rd day after (8 February) is a rest day, so the 2nd day after (7 February).
#ASSERT `s 22 the last day on which the total salary and any sum due must be paid` (Date 5 2 2026) TRUE (LIST Date 8 2 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 7 2 2026)
-- not possible; no rest days or holidays: the 3rd day after.
#ASSERT `s 22 the last day on which the total salary and any sum due must be paid` (Date 5 2 2026) TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 8 2 2026)
-- 7 and 8 February are not days for payment: the 1st day after.
#ASSERT `s 22 the last day on which the total salary and any sum due must be paid` (Date 5 2 2026) TRUE (LIST Date 7 2 2026, Date 8 2 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 6 2 2026)
-- every one of the 3 days is a rest day or holiday: the text gives no later day.
#ASSERT `s 22 the last day on which the total salary and any sum due must be paid` (Date 5 2 2026) TRUE (LIST Date 6 2 2026, Date 7 2 2026, Date 8 2 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- arguments: day of dismissal, day paid, not possible on that day, the rest days and holidays.
#ASSERT `s 22 the total salary and any sum due was paid on the day of dismissal or, if that was not possible, within 3 days after, on a day that is not a rest day or holiday` (Date 5 2 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) FALSE (LIST Date 8 2 2026)
#ASSERT `s 22 the total salary and any sum due was paid on the day of dismissal or, if that was not possible, within 3 days after, on a day that is not a rest day or holiday` (Date 5 2 2026) (Date 7 2 2026) TRUE (LIST Date 8 2 2026)
-- paid on the rest day itself: not a day the section allows.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 22 the total salary and any sum due was paid on the day of dismissal or, if that was not possible, within 3 days after, on a day that is not a rest day or holiday` (Date 5 2 2026) (Date 8 2 2026) TRUE (LIST Date 8 2 2026))
-- the 4th day after.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 22 the total salary and any sum due was paid on the day of dismissal or, if that was not possible, within 3 days after, on a day that is not a rest day or holiday` (Date 5 2 2026) (Date 9 2 2026) TRUE EMPTY)
-- it was possible to pay on the day, and the employer paid a day later: not allowed.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 22 the total salary and any sum due was paid on the day of dismissal or, if that was not possible, within 3 days after, on a day that is not a rest day or holiday` (Date 5 2 2026) (Date 6 2 2026) FALSE EMPTY)
#TRACE `s 22 the employer's duty to pay on dismissal` 0 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 22 the employer` DOES `s 22 pay the total salary and any sum due to the dismissed employee` AT 0
#TRACE `s 22 the employer's duty to pay on dismissal` 3 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 22 the employer` DOES `s 22 pay the total salary and any sum due to the dismissed employee` AT 4

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 23 Payment on termination by employee`
-- (1): arguments are: terminates under section 11 or after due notice, the day terminated, the day paid.
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the total salary due was paid on the day on which the contract of service was terminated` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the total salary due was paid on the day on which the contract of service was terminated` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(1) the total salary due was paid on the day on which the contract of service was terminated` FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 23(1) the employer's duty to pay on the day the contract of service is terminated` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 23(1) the employer` DOES `s 23(1) pay the total salary due to the employee on the day on which the contract of service is terminated` AT 0
#TRACE `s 23(1) the employer's duty to pay on the day the contract of service is terminated` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 23(1) the employer` DOES `s 23(1) pay the total salary due to the employee on the day on which the contract of service is terminated` AT 1
-- (2): the employee terminated on Monday 2 March 2026; the 7th day after is Monday 9 March.
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the last day before the expiry of which the total salary due must be paid` (Date 2 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 9 3 2026)
-- terminated on Saturday 7 March 2026: the 7th day after is Saturday 14 March; if that is a public holiday, the Monday, 16 March.
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the last day before the expiry of which the total salary due must be paid` (Date 7 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the last day before the expiry of which the total salary due must be paid` (Date 7 3 2026) (LIST Date 14 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 16 3 2026)
-- arguments: without notice or without waiting, the day terminated, the day paid, public holidays.
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the total salary due was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the day on which the employee terminated the contract of service` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the total salary due was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the day on which the employee terminated the contract of service` TRUE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not that kind of termination: subsection (1) governs, and (2) is silent.
#ASSERT `s 23(2) the total salary due was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the day on which the employee terminated the contract of service` FALSE (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 23(2) the employer's duty to pay after the employee terminates without notice` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 23(2) the employer` DOES `s 23(2) pay the total salary due to the employee` AT 7
#TRACE `s 23(2) the employer's duty to pay after the employee terminates without notice` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 23(2) the employer` DOES `s 23(2) pay the total salary due to the employee` AT 8
-- (3): the employer may deduct the sum in lieu of notice, unless a court or the Commissioner has ordered otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 23(3) the most the employer may deduct from the salary due to the employee` FALSE (JUST 500) EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 23(3) the most the employer may deduct from the salary due to the employee` TRUE (JUST 500) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(3) the most the employer may deduct from the salary due to the employee` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 24 Income tax clearance`
-- (1): no payment without the Comptroller's permission.
#ASSERT `s 24(1) payment of the salary or other sum due on termination of service is to be made to the employee by the employer` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- with permission the subsection permits no payment by itself, and sections 22 and 23 say when payment is due.
#ASSERT `s 24(1) payment of the salary or other sum due on termination of service is to be made to the employee by the employer` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the prohibition: paying without permission is a breach (read the trace); with permission the prohibition does not arise.
#TRACE `s 24(1) the employer's prohibition on paying without the Comptroller's permission` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 24(1) the employer` DOES `s 24(1) pay the salary or other sum due to the employee on termination of service without the Comptroller's permission` AT 5
-- (2): the Comptroller received notice on Sunday 1 March 2026; the 30th day after is Tuesday 31 March.
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the last day by which the payment of the salary or other sum due must be made` (Date 1 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2026)
-- if 31 March is a public holiday: Wednesday 1 April.
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the last day by which the payment of the salary or other sum due must be made` (Date 1 3 2026) (LIST Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 4 2026)
-- arguments: the day the notice was received, the day paid, public holidays.
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the payment was not delayed more than 30 days after the notice was given to and received by the Comptroller` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24(2) the payment was not delayed more than 30 days after the notice was given to and received by the Comptroller` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EMPTY EQUALS JUST FALSE
#TRACE `s 24(2) the employer's duty to give the Comptroller notice immediately` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 24(2) the employer` DOES `s 24(2) give notice of the termination of service to the Comptroller of Income Tax` AT 0
#TRACE `s 24(2) the employer's duty to give the Comptroller notice immediately` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 24(2) the employer` DOES `s 24(2) give notice of the termination of service to the Comptroller of Income Tax` AT 2

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 25 Payment to be made during working hours`
-- arguments: on a working day, during working hours, at the place of work or an agreed place.
#ASSERT `s 25(1) the payment of salary was made on a working day and during working hours at the place of work or at an agreed place` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25(1) the payment of salary was made on a working day and during working hours at the place of work or at an agreed place` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25(1) the payment of salary was made on a working day and during working hours at the place of work or at an agreed place` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 25(1) the payment of salary was made on a working day and during working hours at the place of work or at an agreed place` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (2): paid into a bank account in Singapore in the employee's name: subsection (1) does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 25(2) subsection (1) applies to the payment of the salary` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not so paid: subsection (2) does not say that (1) applies; (1) does so itself.
-- s 25(2): payment not into a Singapore bank account: (2) does not apply, and (1) is a general rule, so (1) applies (read both, 2026-11-05).
#ASSERT `s 25(2) subsection (1) applies to the payment of the salary` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
